    "en": {
      "caveats": "The model's performance and cost-reduction claims are based on operational simulations rather than a real-world deployment.",
      "what": "The study develops a location and size optimization model for emergency medical service (EMS) stations that applies distinct planning parameters to urban and rural areas. The model was validated in Zhengzhou, China, using multi-source big data including population mobility and time-dependent traffic across multiple daily time periods to optimize the distribution of stations, ambulances, and crews.",
